1
00:00:02,130 --> 00:00:05,670
Hello English learners and welcome to EnglishPod.

2
00:00:05,950 --> 00:00:06,630
My name is Marco.

3
00:00:07,090 --> 00:00:07,570
I'm Amira.

4
00:00:07,930 --> 00:00:13,190
Amira and I are here today with an interesting lesson about a hotel situation.

5
00:00:13,830 --> 00:00:16,210
Amira, why don't you give us a little bit more information?

6
00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:25,210
Well, the situation is taking place in a hotel and someone is checking in and is obtaining an upgrade.

7
00:00:25,710 --> 00:00:28,510
An upgrade, okay, that's an interesting word.

8
00:00:29,090 --> 00:00:34,530
Why don't we listen to the dialogue and then we'll come back and explain all this vocabulary.

9
00:00:42,860 --> 00:00:43,260
Good afternoon.

10
00:00:43,860 --> 00:00:44,740
What can I do for you?

11
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:46,400
I'd like to check in please.

12
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:49,200
I have a reservation under the name Anthony Roberts.

13
00:00:50,110 --> 00:00:50,770
All right.

14
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:52,680
Roberts.

15
00:00:53,230 --> 00:00:55,850
Oh, Mr. Roberts, we've been expecting you.

16
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:58,970
And here is your key card to the presidential suite.

17
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:01,810
But there must be some mistake.

18
00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:03,650
My reservation was for a standard room.

19
00:01:04,290 --> 00:01:04,990
Are you sure?

20
00:01:05,690 --> 00:01:06,470
Let me double check.

21
00:01:07,110 --> 00:01:09,170
Yeah, here, this is my confirmation number.

22
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:12,060
You're right, Mr. Roberts.

23
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:14,260
There seems to be a mix up.

24
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:16,660
Unfortunately, we're overbooked at the moment.

25
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:19,560
So?

26
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:20,710
Not to worry.

27
00:01:21,440 --> 00:01:23,650
We're pleased to offer you a complimentary upgrade.

28
00:01:25,720 --> 00:01:30,880
Presidential suite, baby!

29
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:36,100
Okay, everyone, that is nice, huh?

30
00:01:36,360 --> 00:01:40,620
Yeah, the guy is really excited that he's gonna get the presidential suite.

31
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:44,640
Yes, there's some interesting phrases and vocabulary items here.

32
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:48,000
And I know, Marco, you want to talk about some of them.

33
00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:54,520
Right, the first one, and this is really useful for all of our listeners who travel a lot.

34
00:01:55,060 --> 00:02:00,300
This phrase will come in handy and it is, I have a reservation under the name.

35
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:02,080
Under the name.

36
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:03,860
Under the name.

37
00:02:04,720 --> 00:02:05,520
Under the name.

38
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:16,460
So before we explain this phrase, let's listen to some examples on how it is used in other situations and then we'll come back and give you more information.

39
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:48,720
Alright some really good examples there on how we could use this phrase in other situations.

40
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:52,380
But just in case, let me explain it real fast.

41
00:02:53,140 --> 00:03:06,460
Under the name means that when you go to the restaurant or a hotel and you tell them your name, they know that you are the person that they have been expecting, they have been waiting.

42
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:08,080
Yes.

43
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:13,420
Well, I have chosen another useful phrase for you and it is mix up.

44
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:14,600
Mix up.

45
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:16,100
Mix up.

46
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:18,080
Mix up.

47
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:19,590
There seems to be a mix up.

48
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:25,670
Before we talk about this phrase, let's listen to some examples of how it is used.

49
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:37,760
There was a mix up at the airport and my bags were sent to Antarctica.

50
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:49,720
I'm sorry sir, there's been a terrible mix up.

51
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:58,600
We've given you the wrong baby.

52
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:00,410
Okay that was useful and funny.

53
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:02,690
Yeah, that's the baby situation.

54
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:03,870
Oh my god.

55
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:05,200
I can't imagine that happening.

56
00:04:05,470 --> 00:04:06,050
Yeah, I know.

57
00:04:06,330 --> 00:04:11,370
Well guys, so a mix up is a confusion or a misunderstanding.

58
00:04:12,650 --> 00:04:13,730
Exactly, well put.

59
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:16,560
Alright Marco, what do you have for us?

60
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:21,030
Okay, the next word that we should take a look at is overbooked.

61
00:04:22,190 --> 00:04:22,670
Overbooked.

62
00:04:23,330 --> 00:04:23,810
Overbooked.

63
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:24,920
Overbooked.

64
00:04:24,990 --> 00:04:26,050
What does that mean?

65
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:32,000
So if a hotel or a flight is overbooked, it means that they are full.

66
00:04:32,620 --> 00:04:33,780
They are more than full.

67
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:37,080
Right, so they cannot accept any more people.

68
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:37,860
Exactly.

69
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:41,960
Okay, now why is this phrase useful?

70
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:44,840
Because it happens all the time.

71
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:52,590
There's so many other situations where you can use this word or hear it from other native English speakers.

72
00:04:52,590 --> 00:04:57,890
For example, a bus or a train can be overbooked.

73
00:04:58,010 --> 00:04:59,790
Exactly, that's really common.

74
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:06,570
Okay, let's take a look at the last phrase for today and that is complimentary upgrade.

75
00:05:10,270 --> 00:05:11,120
Complimentary upgrade.

76
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:11,570
Complimentary upgrade.

77
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:13,550
Complimentary upgrade.

78
00:05:14,420 --> 00:05:27,930
So this means that, for example, when the hotel is overbooked and all of their standard rooms are full, they will give you a better room, a more expensive room, but free.

79
00:05:28,510 --> 00:05:30,230
Yes, because it was not your fault.

80
00:05:30,990 --> 00:05:36,110
Right, this also happens sometimes, if you're lucky, on airplane flights.

81
00:05:36,510 --> 00:05:36,790
Yes.

82
00:05:37,130 --> 00:05:47,270
So if you are in economy class and an airplane, but for some reason it's overbooked, they will move you to business class or first class for free.

83
00:05:47,690 --> 00:05:50,930
I have a similar story, but I'm not going to tell you about it now.

84
00:05:51,370 --> 00:05:57,990
For now, let's go and listen to the dialogue one more time and when we come back, we'll talk some more.

85
